  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up building energy efficiency in Mongolia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to mobilize investment to scale-up retrofitting to reduce building heat loss, save energy, reduce GHG emissions and air pollutants, and improve the comfort and well-being of building residents.  Estimated USD 100-125 million required to retrofit all 730 buildings at sub-national level with full scope &#x2013; walls, windows, roof and basement (construction costs and materials have increased significantly as a result of covid). Final design of the financial mechanism will need to consider level of financial contribution from households at sub-national level. In some of the bigger cities where 75% of the apartments are located households should have the capacity to contribute, but in smaller towns their incomes may be lower making it difficult for households to contribute at the same level.</narrative>
  </description>
